  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Nevada has received $3.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state saw obligations fall 22.5% year over year while procurement activity included 20,466 awards with an average award size of $153K. Fiscal-year trends show obligations peaked at $4B in FY24 and FY25, then moved to $3.1B in FY26. Buying agencies concentrate spending: the Department of Defense obligated $1.2B and the Department of Energy obligated $1.1B in the current fiscal year to date. Vendors with the largest obligations include MISSION SUPPORT & TEST SERVICES LLC at $997M and FLEET VEHICLE SOURCE INC at $452M. Facilities Support Services leads industries with $1.1B in obligations, followed by Engineering Services at $613M and Automobile Manufacturing at $452M. These figures are contract obligations and the FY2026 totals are partial, fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are buying the most in Nevada?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.2B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Energy obligated $1.1B. The General Services Administration, Department of Veterans Affairs, and Department of the Interior follow with $539M, $90.2M, and $82.1M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest contractors and which industries dominate?",
        "body": "MISSION SUPPORT & TEST SERVICES LLC received $997M in obligations, followed by FLEET VEHICLE SOURCE INC at $452M and JT4 LLC at $383M. Facilities Support Services is the largest industry with $1.1B, Engineering Services is next with $613M, and Automobile Manufacturing accounts for $452M."
      }
    ]
  },
